	<item>
		<title><![CDATA[The long road north]]></title>
		<link>http://wp-theme-sierra-madre.local/the-long-road-north/</link>
		<pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator>admin</dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://wp-theme-sierra-madre.local/?p=302</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph {"dropCap":true} -->
<p class="has-drop-cap">Three days on the road north is long enough to forget what flat ground feels like. The rain arrives in sheets, then softens into mist that hangs between the pines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Towns appear as brief brightness — a market, a church facade, steam from coffee — then fold back into the ridge. By the second afternoon we had stopped asking how much farther.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What remains is the sound of water in the gullies and the sense that the mountains are reading us as carefully as we are reading them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Three days through rain, mountain roads and towns that disappear into cloud before noon.]]></excerpt:encoded>
